  "reading": "leaked rows share a clip with the fit, so the refit has seen near-duplicates of them; a leaked score better than the clean score is the leak flattering the reported holdout, independent of what the aggregate number did. 'clean' here is ROW LEVEL: these rows' own latents come from held-out clips only. It does not mean their activations are independent of the fit -- the rows are mlp_in after several DiT layers whose attention receptive field is the whole batch row, so unless the window is clip-aligned (one clip per batch row) a clean row's activation is still a function of the fit clips beside it. The count row_level_clean_rows_whose_receptive_field_still_touches_a_fit_clip says how many.",
